1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Tanya Cushman Reviewer: Peter van de Ven
Tanya Cushman评论者： Peter van de Ven

2
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:20,640
Hear that?
你听到了吗？

3
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:23,640
That's nothing.
没关系。

4
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:28,400
Which is what I, as a speaker at today's conference,
这就是我，作为今天会议的发言人，

5
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:29,600
have for you all.
为你们所有人准备好。

6
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:37,080
I have nothing, nada, zip, zilch, zippo.
我什么都没有， nada ， zip ， zilch ， zippo。

7
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:40,560
Nothing smart, nothing inspirational,
没有什么聪明，没有什么鼓舞人心的，

8
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:42,880
nothing even remotely researched at all.
甚至没有任何远程研究。

9
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:46,480
I have absolutely nothing to say whatsoever.
我完全没有什么可说的。

10
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:51,280
And yet, through my manner of speaking, I will make it seem like I do.
然而，通过我的说话方式，我会让它看起来像我一样。

11
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:55,720
Like what I am saying is brilliant.
就像我说的很精彩。

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,080
You've learned something.
你学到了一些东西。

13
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:05,000
Now, I'm going to get started with the opening.
现在，我将从开场白开始。

14
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:06,680
I'm going to make a lot of hand gestures.
我会做很多手势。

15
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:08,360
I'm going to do this with my right hand.
我要用右手来做这件事。

16
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:09,560
I'm going to do this with my left.
我要用我的左手来做这件事。

17
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:11,120
I'm going to adjust my glasses.
我要调整我的眼镜。

18
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:13,640
And then I'm going to ask you all a question.
然后我要问大家一个问题。

19
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:16,240
By show of hands, how many of you all have been asked a question before?
举手，你们中有多少人曾经被问过问题？

20
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:19,160
Okay, great.
很好 不错

21
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:19,920
I'm seeing some hands.
我看到一些手。

22
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:21,040
And again, I have nothing here.
再说一遍，我这里什么都没有。

23
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:26,920
Now, I'm going to react to that and act like I'm telling you a personal anecdote.
现在，我要对此做出反应，表现得好像我在告诉你一个个人轶事。

24
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:29,400
Something to break the tension.
打破紧张气氛的东西。

25
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:31,840
Something to endear myself a little bit.
让自己有点爱惜的东西。

26
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:35,400
Something kind of embarrassing.
有点尴尬。

27
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:39,880
And you guys are going to make an aw sound.
你们会发出一个aw的声音。

28
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:42,160
It's true.
这是真的。

29
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:43,000
It really happened.
真的发生了。

30
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:46,880
And now, I'm going to bring it to a broader point.
现在，我将把它带到一个更广泛的点。

31
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:48,440
I'm going to reel you back in.
我要把你卷回去。

32
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:51,320
I'm going to make it intellectual.
会成功。

33
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:53,840
I'm going to bring it to this man right here.
我要把它带到这里给这个人。

34
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:59,000
Now, what this man did was important, I'm sure.
现在，这个人的所作所为很重要，我敢肯定。

35
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:03,620
But I, for one, have no idea who he is.
但是我不知道他是谁。

36
00:02:04,340 --> 00:02:06,840
I simply Google image the word scientist.
我只是在谷歌上搜索“科学家”这个词。

37
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:11,180
And now, you see, I'd like it to seem like I'm making points,
现在，你看，我希望它看起来像我正在做点，

38
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:15,140
building an argument, inspiring you to change your life.
建立一个论点，激励你改变你的生活。

39
00:02:15,460 --> 00:02:20,960
When in reality, this is just me buying time.
实际上，这只是我在争取时间。

40
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:23,900
Now, if you don't believe me, let's take a look at the numbers.
现在，如果你不相信我，让我们来看看数字。

41
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:25,460
This is a real thing that's happening right now.
这是现在正在发生的真实情况。

42
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:29,180
The number of talks that I'm giving is one.
我演讲的次数是一次。

43
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:32,900
Interesting facts imparted thus far in said talk.
到目前为止，上述谈话中传达了有趣的事实。

44
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:34,020
Well, that's going to be a zero.
嗯，这将是一个零。

45
00:02:35,060 --> 00:02:37,960
My height in inches is 70.5.
我的身高是70.5英寸。

46
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,080
Note the .5 there.
请注意那里的.5。

47
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:41,240
Two times six equals 12.
2乘以6等于12。

48
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:44,000
And then, interestingly enough, six times two also equals 12.
然后，有趣的是， 6乘以2也等于12。

49
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:44,700
That's math.
这就是数学。

50
00:02:46,760 --> 00:02:49,040
352 is a three-digit number.
352是一个三位数数字。

51
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,340
One, two, three, four, five.
一，二，三，四，五……

52
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:54,080
And then, almost immediately following that, we get six, seven, eight, nine, ten.
然后，几乎紧接着，我们得到六，七，八，九，十。

53
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:59,620
Now, to add more filler here, I'm going to give you a couple more numbers to consider.
现在，为了在这里添加更多填充物，我将再给您几个数字来考虑。

54
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:13,200
118, 237, 5,601, 2.6 million, 4, 4, 24, staggering.
118, 237, 5,601, 260万, 4, 4, 24,惊人。

55
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:16,640
These are real numbers, all of them.
这些都是实数，全部都是。

56
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:20,260
And to follow that up, let's take a look at some graphs.
接下来，我们来看一些图表。

57
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:23,580
Now, if you take a look at this pie chart, what you're going to see is that the majority
现在，如果你看一下这个饼图，你会看到大多数

58
00:03:23,580 --> 00:03:25,180
far exceeds the minority.
远远超过了少数民族。

59
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:27,220
Everybody see that?
大家都看到了吗？

60
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:29,100
Cool, isn't it?
很酷，不是吗？

61
00:03:29,780 --> 00:03:33,820
And let's take a look at this bar graph because it shows, similarly, irrelevant data.
让我们来看看这个条形图，因为它同样显示了不相关的数据。

62
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:38,820
Now, I'm doing this because I'd like to make it seem like I've done my homework.
现在，我这样做是因为我想让它看起来像我已经完成了我的家庭作业。

63
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:44,060
If you were, say, watching this on YouTube with the sound off, you might think, huh, okay.
如果你在YouTube上关掉声音看这个，你可能会想，嗯，好吧。

64
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:46,340
This guy knows what he's talking about.
这家伙知道自己在说什么。

65
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:48,100
But I don't.
但 我並 不介意

66
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:50,440
I'm floundering, panicking.
我挣扎着，惊慌失措。

67
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:51,160
I've got nothing.
我什么也没有钓到。

68
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:53,080
I'm a total and utter phony.
我是一个彻头彻尾的骗子。

69
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:54,520
But you know what?
但 你們 知道 麼

70
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:56,400
I was offered a TED Talk.
有人邀请我做TED演讲。

71
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:58,760
And, damn it, I'm going to see it through.
而且，该死的，我会看到它通过。

72
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:06,780
Now, if you take a look behind me, these are just words paired with vaguely thought-provoking
现在，如果你看看我身后，这些只是与模糊发人深省的单词配对

73
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:07,580
stock photos.
库存照片

74
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:12,160
I'm going to point at them like I'm making use both of my time as well as your time.
我会指着他们，就像我在利用我的时间和你的时间一样。

75
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:14,820
But in reality, I don't know what half of them mean.
但实际上，我不知道其中一半是什么意思。

76
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:18,540
And now, as these continue, I'm just going to start saying gibberish.
现在，随着这些继续，我将开始说胡言乱语。

77
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:21,000
Wag-a-wah, gabba-gabba.
Wag-a-wah, gabba-gabba.

78
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:23,540
Turkey, mouth-in-a-mouth.
土耳其，口口相传。

79
00:04:24,420 --> 00:04:26,500
Chip, trip, my dog Skip.
薯片，绊倒，我的狗跳过。

80
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:28,420
Rip it and dip it, Richard.
撕开它，蘸上它，理查德。

81
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:32,420
I'm an itty-bitty baby bopper, and I'm hungry in my tum-tum.
我是一个非常小的婴儿bopper ，我在我的肚子里饿了。

82
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:35,240
Brad Pitt, Uma Thurman.
Brad Pitt ， Uma Thurman。

83
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:39,860
Names, things, words, words, and more things.
名称、事物、词语、词语和更多事物。

84
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:42,360
And see, it feels like it might make sense, doesn't it?
你看，感觉这可能是有道理的，不是吗？

85
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:47,100
Like maybe, just maybe, I'm building to some sort of satisfying conclusion.
也许，只是也许，我正在建立某种令人满意的结论。

86
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:49,000
I mean, I'm gesticulating as though I am.
我的意思是，我在做手势，就好像我在做手势一样。

87
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:51,080
I'm pacing, I'm growing in intensity.
我在节奏，我的强度在增长。

88
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:53,600
I'm taking off my glasses, which, by the way, are just frames.
我要摘下我的眼镜，顺便说一下，这只是镜框。

89
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:05,280
I wore them to look smart, even though my vision is perfect.
我穿着它们看起来很聪明，尽管我的视力很完美。

90
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,200
And now I'm going to slow things down a little bit.
现在我要把速度放慢一点。

91
00:05:10,140 --> 00:05:11,180
I'm going to change the tone.
我要改变语气。

92
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:17,260
I'm going to make it seem like I'm building to a moment.
我会让它看起来像我在建造一瞬间。

93
00:05:20,540 --> 00:05:21,840
And what if I was?
如果我是呢？

94
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:25,500
Amazing, isn't it?
太棒了，不是吗？

95
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:26,240
What can you do?
您能做什么？

96
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:27,960
Life's a roller coaster.
生活就像过山车。

97
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:35,780
You know, if there's one thing you take away from my talk,
你知道，如果你从我的演讲中学到了一件事，

98
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:37,540
I'd like you to think about what you heard at the beginning.
我希望您想想您一开始听到的内容。

99
00:05:38,540 --> 00:05:40,800
And I'd like you to think about what you hear now.
我想让你想想你现在听到了什么。

100
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:45,460
Because it was nothing, and it's still nothing.
因为它什么都不是，它仍然什么都不是。

101
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:46,240
Think about that.
想想看，不是么？

102
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:48,540
Or don't, that's fine.
或者不要，没关系。

103
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:51,740
And now I'm going to stop talking.
现在我要停止说话了。

104
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:52,760
Thank you.
谢谢。
